      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 6.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "So, hello, doctor. It's my turn, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.72,
      "end_seconds": 12.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "that's alright, take a seat tell me why you've come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.97,
      "end_seconds": 19.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "so, I've been feeling cold all the time, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.93,
      "end_seconds": 28.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "so, is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.38,
      "end_seconds": 32.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "About... well, nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.75,
      "end_seconds": 37.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.84,
      "end_seconds": 43.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Constipation goes along with it, um, most of the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.78,
      "end_seconds": 47.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Has there been dry skin too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.21,
      "end_seconds": 53.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Yeah, that too. With dry skin, moisturiser helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.37,
      "end_seconds": 76.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "what medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.03,
      "end_seconds": 83.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.21,
      "end_seconds": 87.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Is there anything medical in your background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.15,
      "end_seconds": 91.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I've got low haemoglobin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.87,
      "end_seconds": 100.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Okay, I can see low haemoglobin in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.07,
      "end_seconds": 120.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.44,
      "end_seconds": 135.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "I play badminton on Sundays. I skip breakfast most days. I run a small shop, so I'm on my feet a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.38,
      "end_seconds": 144.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.49,
      "end_seconds": 152.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Well, yes, I had a a lump removed from my back, years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.55,
      "end_seconds": 158.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Have you had any low mood or hair loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.03,
      "end_seconds": 169.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "no low mood or hair loss, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.51,
      "end_seconds": 175.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "Have you had any heavy periods or swelling in the neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.17,
      "end_seconds": 181.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "None, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.18,
      "end_seconds": 186.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "on the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.82,
      "end_seconds": 190.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "no, um, nothing with my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.29,
      "end_seconds": 193.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.88,
      "end_seconds": 196.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.17,
      "end_seconds": 198.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Let's do your observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.45,
      "end_seconds": 213.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.89,
      "end_seconds": 245.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.37,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 124 over 82, temperature 36.4, SpO2 97 percent on room air, respiratory rate 14, pulse is 83 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.45,
      "end_seconds": 248.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.64,
      "end_seconds": 252.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I'll explain what that means shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.48,
      "end_seconds": 257.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "if you're comfortable, I'll examine you now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.77,
      "end_seconds": 261.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "no problem"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.84,
      "end_seconds": 265.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Take your time, no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.59,
      "end_seconds": 275.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "reflexes are a bit slow to relax"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.28,
      "end_seconds": 287.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "right, you can sit back down so, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with an underactive thyroid"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.93,
      "end_seconds": 292.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Hmm, is this gonna go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.92,
      "end_seconds": 316.46,
      "duration_seconds": 22.54,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's an underactive thyroid, and we'll know more once the a thyroid test is back. a thyroid test is what I'd like next, for hypothyroid symptoms. We should do blood tests for fatigue. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.12,
      "end_seconds": 351.5,
      "duration_seconds": 34.38,
      "text": "We'll begin with levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning on an empty stomach, until we review. You take it by mouth. That should help with hypothyroidism. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Take the thyroid tablet on an empty stomach, half an hour before breakfast, and not with calcium or iron. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.34,
      "end_seconds": 364.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse okay, call the clinic if you need us"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.2,
      "end_seconds": 367.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Thanks, that was helpful."
    }
  ]
